To generate an automatically generated table of contents (TOC) in LaTeX, follow these steps:

1. Add the `toc` package to your preamble:

```
\usepackage{toc}
```

2. Use the `\tableofcontents` command in your document, typically placed after the `\begin{document}` command:

```
\begin{document}
\tableofcontents
```

3. Add the `\section`, `\subsection`, or `\subsubsection` commands to your document to create the content for the TOC. For example:

```
\section{Introduction}
\subsection{Background}
\subsubsection{History}

\section{Methodology}
\subsection{Data Collection}
\subsubsection{Data Analysis}
```

4. Compile your document using LaTeX. This will generate a TOC at the beginning of your document, automatically formatted based on the sectioning commands used.

Here's an example of a complete LaTeX document with an automatically generated TOC:

```latex
\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{toc}

\begin{document}
\tableofcontents

\section{Introduction}
\subsection{Background}
\subsubsection{History}

\section{Methodology}
\subsection{Data Collection}
\subsubsection{Data Analysis}

\end{document}
``` 

When you compile this document, you should see a TOC at the beginning, like this:

```
Contents
1. Introduction
   1.1 Background
      1.1.1 History
2. Methodology
   2.1 Data Collection
   2.2 Data Analysis
```

