```java
public class PowerOfThree {

    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        double logValue = Math.log10(n) / Math.log10(3);
        return (logValue % 1 == 0);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 27;
        boolean result = new PowerOfThree().isPowerOfThree(n);
        System.out.println(result); // true

        n = 0;
        result = new PowerOfThree().isPowerOfThree(n);
        System.out.println(result); // false

        n = -1;
        result = new PowerOfThree().isPowerOfThree(n);
        System.out.println(result); // false
    }
}
```

The algorithm works as follows:

1. Check if the input is non-negative, otherwise return false.
2. Compute the logarithm of the input number base 3 using `Math.log10(n) / Math.log10(3)`.
3. Check if the result is an integer, i.e., there is no fractional part. If it is an integer, then n is a power of three, otherwise it's not.

This solution has a time complexity of O(1) and does not use loops or recursion.

